  "name": " HIV VIRAL LOAD",
  "code": "HIV",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>An HIV viral load test is a blood test that measures the amount of HIV virus in the bloodstream. The test result indicates how much virus is present in the blood and is used to monitor the effectiveness of antiretroviral therapy (ART) and to track the progression of HIV infection.</p><p>The interpretation of an HIV viral load test result is based on the number of copies of HIV RNA detected in a milliliter of blood. The lower the number of copies, the better the response to treatment.</p>",
